{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Serena Williams tennis career began at 1995 but didn't compete in 1996.","title":"Serena Williams's early career"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She continued through the 1997 season and ended in the top 20 in 1998.","title":"Serena Williams's early career"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Mariaan de Swardt won in the final 3–6, 7–6, 7–5 against Barbara Schett.","title":"1998 Boston Cup – Singles"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Serena Williams has won dozens of Grand Slam singles titles, multiple Olympic gold medals, held the world No. 1 ranking and completed a Career Doubles Grand Slam, whereas Mariaan de Swardt is only noted as a doubles finalist at the 1998 Boston Cup.
Evidence: {"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Williams sisters are two professional American tennis players: Venus Williams (b. 1980), a seven-time Grand Slam title winner (singles), and Serena Williams (b. 1981), twenty-three-time Grand Slam title winner (singles), both of whom were coached from an early age by their parents Richard Williams and Oracene Price.","title":"Williams sisters"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":2,"text":" They became the first two players, female or male, to play in 4 consecutive grand slam singles finals from the 2002 French Open to the 2003 Australian Open; Serena famously won all 4 to complete the first of two \"Serena Slams\".","title":"Williams sisters"}
Evidence: {"sentence_id":3,"text":" Between 2000 and 2016, a 17-year span, they collectively won 12 Wimbledon singles titles (Venus won 5 and"],"previous_answer":"Serena Williams reached the top 20 and had a longer, more successful career, while Mariaan de Swardt’s record in the evidence is limited to a single tournament win.","question":"Why is Serena Williams more accomplished than Mariaan de Swardt in her tennis career?"}
